{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve had this cough for about a day now. It’s worse than usual—bringing up yellow mucus. And today, I started feeling really nauseous and threw up five times."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever, shortness of breath, or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever or trouble breathing. But my stomach hurts—probably from coughing so much. I did get a runny nose today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Your vitals show your heart rate is a bit high, and your blood pressure is elevated. We’ll run some tests to see what’s going on. Did you take anything for the nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I tried an over-the-counter cough suppressant. The ER gave me Zofran and Ativan, which helped a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll continue those to help control the nausea. You also got a chest X-ray. It shows no pneumonia—your lungs look clear. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not pneumonia? I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, no signs of infection in your lungs. The cough and mucus are likely from a viral upper respiratory infection. We won’t need antibiotics for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ve had a mild cough for a while, but this one feels different."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the increased phlegm suggests a new viral trigger. We’ll focus on symptom relief. Your blood work shows your kidney function is a bit worse than usual—creatinine is 2.4."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s not good. My baseline is around 1.8. Could the vomiting be affecting that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Dehydration from vomiting can stress the kidneys. We’re starting IV fluids to help. We also held your lisinopril for now—it can affect kidney function when you’re dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I understand. What about my potassium? I remember last time it was high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your first potassium was high, but the sample was hemolyzed—meaning it might not be accurate. The repeat was 5.5, which is mildly elevated. No EKG changes, so we gave Kayexalate to bring it down safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember Kayexalate from last time. It’s not the most pleasant, but I’ll take it if it helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor it closely. Your insulin and diabetes meds are continuing as usual—glargine twice daily and sliding scale for meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My A1c was 7.9 last time—trying to keep it under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a solid number. We’ll keep an eye on your sugars. Your pain regimen—gabapentin, oxycodone, morphine—is continuing, but we lowered gabapentin to 300mg daily due to your kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s fine. I’ve been managing the phantom pain okay. Just want to make sure it doesn’t get worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep it controlled. You also had a urine test—showed signs of possible infection, so we sent a culture."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I get those often. Last time it was Klebsiella. They gave me cipro in the ER—should I keep taking it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just one dose for now. The culture came back mixed flora—likely contamination from stool. So we’re not treating it as a real UTI unless it changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, that makes sense. I catheterize four times a day—sometimes it’s hard to keep everything sterile."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2143-03-23 17:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep doing straight catheterizations as needed. Blood cultures were drawn and are pending—just to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2143-03-24 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2143-03-24 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Haven’t thrown up since yesterday. Still coughing, but not as bad. My stomach feels better too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2143-03-24 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. Your heart rate has come down—no longer in tachycardia. IV fluids are helping with hydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2143-03-24 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel less shaky. Is my kidney function improving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2143-03-24 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, creatinine is trending down to 2.1. We’ll keep monitoring. We also did an abdominal X-ray last night—no blockage or obstruction. Your pain is likely from coughing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2143-03-24 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried something was wrong with my intestines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2143-03-24 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of that. We’re switching your nausea meds to oral Zofran and compazine—you can take them as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2143-03-24 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Can I start eating more than just clear liquids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2143-03-24 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll advance your diet to full meals. Start slow—see how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2143-03-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Blood cultures came back negative—no infection in the blood. That’s excellent news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2143-03-25 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. So the cough and nausea were just from a virus?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2143-03-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. No bacterial infection found. Your creatinine is now 1.9—back near your baseline. We’ll keep gabapentin at 300mg daily and restart lisinopril at a lower dose—5mg once a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2143-03-25 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ll take half of my usual 10mg tablet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2143-03-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re also starting metoprolol 25mg twice daily—important for your heart after your past NSTEMI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2143-03-25 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t have that before. Any side effects I should watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2143-03-25 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might lower your heart rate or blood pressure. We’ll monitor. Most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2143-03-26 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. You’ve been eating full meals, no nausea, and your cough is improving. We’ll plan for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2143-03-26 10:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds will I go home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2143-03-26 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same as before, with a few changes: lower-dose lisinopril, new metoprolol, and reduced gabapentin. We’re also sending Zofran and compazine home in case nausea returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2143-03-26 10:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my insulin? Still 3 units glargine twice daily?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2143-03-26 10:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s correct. Continue your sliding scale with lispro before meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge. Your condition is stable—no coughing fits, no nausea, eating well. Creatinine is 1.9, potassium normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better. Thank you. Do I need to follow up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, see your primary doctor in a week to review meds, especially metoprolol and kidney function. Call if fever, vomiting, or trouble breathing returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll keep an eye on things and take my meds as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing a great job managing your health. We’ll have a nurse go over your discharge instructions and prescriptions now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’re here if you need anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. The discharge team will assist you shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready when they are."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Rest well today, and we’ll get you home soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Our pleasure. Take care of yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ll make the appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Get some rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2143-03-27 11:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2143-03-23 17:07:00",
    "admission_end": "2143-03-27 18:38:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 58-year-old woman with type 1 diabetes, bilateral lower extremity amputations, chronic kidney disease, and systolic heart failure was admitted for cough, nausea, and vomiting. She had a productive cough with yellow phlegm and multiple episodes of non-bilious vomiting. Initial evaluation revealed sinus tachycardia, elevated creatinine (2.4), and mild hyperkalemia (5.5). A chest X-ray showed no pneumonia, and symptoms were attributed to a viral upper respiratory infection. Nausea and vomiting were managed with IV and oral antiemetics, and IV fluids were given for dehydration. Urine cultures showed mixed flora consistent with contamination, and blood cultures were negative. Her kidney function improved to a creatinine of 1.9, and electrolytes normalized. Lisinopril was held during admission due to renal impairment and restarted at a reduced dose (5 mg daily) at discharge. Gabapentin was renally dosed, and metoprolol was initiated for secondary prevention after NSTEMI. She tolerated a full diet, symptoms resolved, and she was discharged home with follow-up instructions.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute upper respiratory infections of unspecified site",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Dehydration",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Hyperkalemia",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Chronic systolic heart failure",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Phantom limb (syndrome)",
      "Neurogenic bladder NOS"
    ]
  }
}
